{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Patch set 2 on change 1924 (commit `d4c72f366c`), responding to the one advisory LLM-Review finding.\n\nFinding: `test_signing_family_keeps_real_headroom` asserted a LOWER LOC bound with no behavioural justification — a behaviour-preserving refactor that legitimately deletes code would fail it. Fair on its strongest point, so the size test is now a CEILING only (<= 500 for all three files), which is the property this ticket actually cares about. The single floor kept is the 100-LOC minimum on the two split-CREATED modules, moved into its own test with the justification stated: it encodes the AGENTS.md rule against splitting a file into stubs, so it is about the shape of the split rather than about file size. Split oracle: 57 passed. `make lint` green.\n\nProcess note: the amend used `git commit --amend -F <file>` and the message file did not carry the `Change-Id`, so the commit-msg hook stamped a fresh one and Gerrit opened a DUPLICATE change 1926. Corrected by restoring Change-Id `I8da07d7e...` onto the commit and re-pushing (now patch set 2 of 1924); **1926 is abandoned** with an explanatory message. Re-pushing outdated the LLM-Review +1 from patch set 1, so both gates are re-running."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787182427644187001,"uuid":"edb38735-0621-4bf8-9b79-4d535f2254db"}